The files data/jailbreakbench.csv (JailbreakBench, Chao et al., NeurIPS 2024
Datasets & Benchmarks) and data/maliciousinstruct.csv (MaliciousInstruct,
Huang et al., ICLR 2024) are redistributed unchanged from the reference
repository; please cite the original works when using them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attribution: in-context-learning circuit (head sets, battery)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

valueheads_pythia/icl_sets.py contains head lists derived from, and a
re-implementation of the census classification rule of, the repository

    andrewgcodes/in-context-learning-circuit
    (commit 26c44caf8f9b5a5a197988095f1f76b0562bbaa4), MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2026 Andrew Gao, William Gao

which accompanies the paper

    "A Circuit for In-Context Learning" - arXiv:2611.05344 (2026).

valueheads_pythia/icl_battery.py contains code adapted from the same
repository (icl/tasks.py: build, mk, NATLAB and the concept-battery loop of
fam_concept / fam_concept12n; icl/tokspans.py: is_bare_ws, label_spans,
target_ids) and a re-implementation of its query-position knockout and
margin scoring (icl/run.py, icl/hooks.py, icl/score.py). The battery data
file data/icl/concept_tasks.json is redistributed unchanged from
batteries/concept_tasks.json at the same commit (sha256
bf242720283bdc9967ffdb22da277f2fc0237d374de2b8214c45790187e60df0).

The per-head census files (data/D188_heads_*.json) are not redistributed; they
are read from a local checkout or downloaded at runtime from that pinned
commit. The original MIT license text of that repository is reproduced below
and applies to the derived and adapted portions and to the redistributed data
file.

